# VTID-03913 — commands actually run.

# --- Investigation (in the prior session turn, VTID-03902 follow-up) ------

# Confirmed the automated operator-planner sweep runs correctly (fires at
# boot, processes real backlog), then found THREE sweep_completed events
# within ~90 seconds — impossible for one process on a 5-min interval:
#   SELECT created_at, topic, status, message, metadata FROM oasis_events
#     WHERE topic = 'operator.planner.sweep_completed'
#     ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 5;
#   -> same handful of VTIDs flap ok:true / ok:false ("spec_insert_failed")
#      across overlapping sweeps -> concurrent processes racing on the
#      same claim.

grep -n "spec_insert_failed\|get_next_spec_version" -A 15 -B 5 \
  services/gateway/src/routes/specs.ts
#   -> Step 2's claim PATCH has no WHERE-condition equivalent (PostgREST
#      filter) on current spec_status -- an unconditional compare-and-swap
#      was never implemented. get_next_spec_version is also non-atomic,
#      but becomes moot once only one caller can ever be "generating" a
#      given vtid at a time.

grep -rn "specs/.*generate\|executeDevGenerateSpec" services/gateway/src \
  --include="*.ts" | grep -v ".test.ts"
#   -> confirmed other callers (dev_generate_spec chat tool, task-intake,
#      email-intake) call this route from states other than 'missing'
#      (e.g. regenerating an existing draft) -- ruled out a
#      spec_status=eq.missing filter, which would have broken legitimate
#      regeneration; landed on spec_status=not.eq.generating instead.

# --- Fix -------------------------------------------------------------

# services/gateway/src/routes/specs.ts
#   Step 2 claim: PATCH ...&spec_status=not.eq.generating with
#   Prefer: return=representation; empty response array => 409
#   already_generating, returned before touching the LLM, the version
#   RPC, the spec insert, or spec_last_error.

# --- Verification ------------------------------------------------------

cd services/gateway

npx jest test/specs-generate-claim.test.ts
#   -> 3/3 new tests passing. (outputs/targeted-tests.txt)

# Mutation check: stripped "&spec_status=not.eq.generating" from the claim
# URL and re-ran the same test file -- confirmed AC-1's test goes red
# (received the plain, unconditional URL) while AC-2/AC-3 still pass
# (a PATCH still "succeeds" unconditionally in that reverted state, so
# only the conditionality assertion catches the regression). Restored the
# fix and re-ran -- all 3 green again.

npx tsc --noEmit
#   -> clean, exit 0. (outputs/tsc.txt)

npx jest
#   -> full suite: 796/797 suites (1 pre-existing skip), 14,212/14,247
#      tests passing, 0 failures. (outputs/full-suite.txt)

